      "Language": "por",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "PURPOSE",
          "content": "To evaluate septal perfusion and contractility in patients with left bundle branch block (LBBB)."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "METHODS",
          "content": "Twenty patients were submitted to myocardial scintigraphy with Tecnecium-99m isontrile after exercise and dipyridamole infusion. The septal contractility was observed during the radionuclide ventriculography. All patients were submitted to coronariography."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "Twenty patients were studied and 17 (85%) had a normal left anterior descending (LAD) artery. Nine (53%) patients had abnormalities in septal perfusion after the exercise and 2 (12%) after dipyridamole infusion. All patients had abnormalities in septal contractility during the radionuclide ventriculography."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSION",
          "content": "The myocardial scintigraphy after dipyridamole infusion showed better specificity in the diagnosis of a LAD lesion. The radionuclide ventriculography was an efficient method to evaluate the septal contraction abnormalities in patients with LBBB."
        }
      ]},
